#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115091 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ecd0f74-19c3-5770-b376-4d945320f06f" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Graph of a Horizontally Reflected Function"}] :question/id #uuid "8bbf173b-820a-5b50-b40f-72e4ef09267a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4977" :question/problem "The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below. Sketch the graph of $y=f(-x)$.\n\n![](images/ca/cafc696543afde5d9e9d6442fa7f5634269ef836d94de40dcac598611be48b8c.png)" :question/worked-solution "To obtain the graph of $y=f(-x)$ from $y=f(x)$, we need to reflect the graph over the $y$-axis. The resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/58/58c9396cfec04e9b042b1dd91d75b0847e34e60fa257866e60ed1b3f37535485.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115092 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6912eee-a9ca-5a57-8564-d276afc29711" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point that Lies on a Transformed Function"}] :question/id #uuid "5b49540d-4bcd-5ba9-b258-d6ad9828f0e7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4981" :question/problem "The point $P$ with coordinates $(1, 2)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x)$. Find a point that must lie on the graph of $y= f(-x)$." :question/worked-solution "The transformation $y=f(-x)$ reflects the curve $y=f(x)$ in the $y$-axis.\n\nFirst, notice that the point $P(1, 2)$ lies $1$ unit to the *right* of the $y$-axis. So, after the transformation is applied and the point is reflected across the $y$-axis, this point will lie $1$ unit to the *left* of the $y$-axis.\n\nTherefore, the point $P'(-1, 2)$ must lie on the graph of $y=f(-x)$.\n\n![](images/0a/0aa23b1c8182d0901e27f9d1df84c30fef44396f6787f370932569f4903fb419.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ecd0f74-19c3-5770-b376-4d945320f06f" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Graph of a Horizontally Reflected Function"}] :ques